<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Hohenlohe-Schillingsfürst</h1><p class="st-meta">1744 CE – 1806 CE · capital Schillingsfürst</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Franconian principality of a Catholic Hohenlohe branch, whose family later produced a German chancellor.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-hohenlohe">Hohenlohe</a> family ruled lands in north-eastern Württemberg and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and divided into many lines. The Catholic Waldenburg branch included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schillingsfurst">Schillingsfürst</a>, on a hill near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rothenburg-ob-der-tauber">Rothenburg</a>, and in 1744 its head was raised to the rank of prince of the Empire.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The principality was small, Catholic and rural, governed from a baroque palace at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schillingsfurst">Schillingsfürst</a>, which still houses a falconry. It belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconian-circle">Franconian Circle</a> and shared the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-hohenlohe">Hohenlohe</a> family's collective vote. Its princes served the emperors in court and army posts.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1806 the principality was mediatised and placed under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bavaria">Kingdom of Bavaria</a>. The family remained prominent: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlodwig-zu-hohenlohe-schillingsfurst">Chlodwig zu Hohenlohe-Schillingsfürst</a> was Bavarian prime minister and German chancellor from 1894 to 1900.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 1744 CE – 1806 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:94.41%;width:1.23%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1744 CE – 1806 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Schillingsfürst</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hohenlohe-Schillingsfürst</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1775&amp;focus=principality-of-hohenlohe-schillingsfurst" aria-label="Principality of Hohenlohe-Schillingsfürst on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4917 459 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Hohenlohe-Schillingsfürst lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5237 715L5219 718M5237 715L5269 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5219 718h0M5269 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5237 715h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5237 715h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Schillingsfürst. <a href="/atlas?year=1775&amp;focus=principality-of-hohenlohe-schillingsfurst">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
